      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The efficacy of a long-term transfusion regimen in preventing sickle cell disease complications is unknown. We examined 17 patients before, during, and after transfusion for cerebral vascular accident and vaso-occlusive crisis. Total hospitalization rate, as well as admissions for vaso-occlusive crisis, cases of acute chest syndrome, and bacterial infections decreased while patients were on a transfusion regimen."},
